{"author":{"id":"ce771b8a9b8c30a8aac165a8b1cdb0957637d3941276ec4f27335daee16d79de"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1795021750,"nonce":"W/bG+Iy/0vQTUT+p3FkkjKJc7aQ=","target":"5a8eb6acbc14acf5257bd3ab92052b5844d6e4c3081943f0e0dc3f26cc5989db","message":"## Parent\n\nSpec: eb1b66f (Environment section rework — grow page)\n\n## What to build\n\nCloses the spec §4.9 gap: log events appear as markers on the environment charts. The per-role history API response gains a markers array containing the role-relevant action-log events inside the requested window — watering, feed and repot events for root-zone roles (soil moisture, pH, EC); light transitions and phase picks for air roles (temperature, humidity, VPD, CO₂). The frontend renders each marker as one quiet vertical tick glyph on the chart, with a tooltip naming the event. A markers on/off toggle in the section header hides and shows all markers at once. Markers are geometry, not colour: no new hues; they respect the Phase Accent Rule. No new endpoints — the existing history endpoint is extended.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] History API response for each role includes in-window markers with the role-relevant event kinds only\n- [ ] Backend integration test seeds a grow with snapshots plus watering/feed/light/phase-pick events and asserts marker selection per role and window filtering\n- [ ] Charts render markers as a single tick glyph; tooltip names the event\n- [ ] Section-header toggle hides/shows markers across all charts\n- [ ] No new hues in chrome; marker styling follows the design system\n- [ ] Both themes verified; chart option-builder unit tests cover marker option generation\n\n## Blocked by\n\n1c69e35 (section skeleton + shared window).","files":null}]}